---
import LaundrySignalGuide from './LaundrySignalGuide.astro'
---

<section id="system-plan" class="system-plan" aria-labelledby="system-plan-title">
  <header class="plan-heading">
    <p class="plan-label">PLANNED ARCHITECTURE / ONE BUILDING</p>
    <h2 id="system-plan-title">From machine readings to a shared view.</h2>
    <p>
      A proposed setup for one building. Equipment selection, purchases, installation and a building pilot are not
      confirmed.
    </p>
  </header>

  <ol class="data-flow" aria-label="Planned data flow">
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <h3>Machine + meter</h3>
      <p>A separate Wi-Fi electricity meter without a relay observes each machine, without switching its power.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <h3>Wi-Fi + HTTPS</h3>
      <p>
        The meter's script sends readings over the building's internet connection using authenticated HTTPS requests.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <h3>Authenticated intake + storage</h3>
      <p>A Supabase Edge Function checks device credentials before storing readings in the database.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <h3>Mobile web app</h3>
      <p>
        Residents see the reported state, its source and freshness. Missing or stale readings mean the state is unknown.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="supporting-inputs">
    <div>
      <h3>Optional manufacturer API</h3>
      <p>
        A supported API may provide cycle or door state. A fresh explicit status takes precedence over an estimate from
        electricity use.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Resident confirmation by QR</h3>
      <p>
        QR labels lead residents to the correct machine for check-in and collection confirmation. Human confirmation
        remains separate from appliance readings.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <LaundrySignalGuide />

  <details class="setup-details">
    <summary>Setup details</summary>
    <p class="setup-intro">A setup plan to validate on site before a building pilot.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Survey the room</strong>
        <p>
          Check appliance models, electrical connections and loads, Wi-Fi coverage and permission to install equipment.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pair and identify each meter</strong>
        <p>Connect each suitable meter to Wi-Fi and assign it to a unique machine ID. Verify the physical mapping.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Configure authenticated reporting</strong>
        <p>
          Prepare HTTPS reporting to the Edge Function with unique, revocable device credentials. Keep database
          privileges and server secrets on the server, outside meter scripts and the browser.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Define state and freshness rules</strong>
        <p>
          Record the source and time of each reading. Define stale-data handling and explicit precedence for a
          supported, fresh manufacturer API. Meter-based rules and thresholds still need validation.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Set up resident access and QR labels</strong>
        <p>
          Restrict access to the building's residents. Match QR labels to machine IDs and verify check-in and collection
          confirmation through that access-controlled flow.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Verify cycles, interruptions and recovery</strong>
        <p>
          Test complete cycles, pauses, power and network outages, and recovery on each supported machine. Detection
          thresholds and timing remain to be determined from those observations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </details>
</section>

<style>
  .system-plan {
    --plan-line: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent);
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 34px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--plan-line);
    min-width: 0;
    font: 15px/1.75 var(--body-font);
    text-shadow: none;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    scroll-margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .system-plan :is(h2, h3, p, ol) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .plan-heading {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .plan-label,
  .step-number {
    font: 11px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
  }
  .plan-heading h2 {
    margin: 12px 0 16px;
    font: 500 clamp(23px, 2.5vw, 30px)/1.35 var(--note-font);
    letter-spacing: -0.6px;
  }
  .system-plan h3 {
    font: 600 15px/1.55 var(--note-font);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  }
  .data-flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .data-flow li {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--plan-line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #39776c 6%, transparent);
  }
  .data-flow li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    right: -20px;
    top: 24px;
    font: 19px/1 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  .step-number {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 17px;
    padding-bottom: 7px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plan-line);
  }
  .data-flow p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .supporting-inputs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 24px 0 34px;
  }
  .supporting-inputs > div {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--plan-line);
  }
  .supporting-inputs p {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .setup-details {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--plan-line);
  }
  .setup-details summary {
    padding: 18px 2px;
    font: 600 15px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .setup-details summary::marker {
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  .setup-details summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .setup-details[open] summary {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .setup-details .setup-intro {
    color: var(--note-color);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .setup-details ol {
    padding: 0 0 8px 24px;
  }
  .setup-details li {
    padding-left: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .setup-details li::marker {
    font: 12px var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  .setup-details li strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .setup-details li p {
    max-width: 76ch;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .data-flow {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .data-flow li {
      padding-left: 58px;
    }
    .data-flow .step-number {
      position: absolute;
      left: 18px;
      top: 18px;
    }
    .data-flow li:not(:last-child)::after {
      content: '↓';
      top: auto;
      bottom: -22px;
      left: 18px;
      right: auto;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .system-plan {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 26px;
    }
    .data-flow,
    .supporting-inputs {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .data-flow li {
      padding: 16px 16px 16px 52px;
    }
    .supporting-inputs {
      gap: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
